  "notes": "A genre-collision producer running three documented project grammars — Major Lazer (dancehall-derived beat with an instrumental hook replacing the chorus), Jack Ü (bass-design-forward) and Silk City (straight four-on-the-floor house with Mark Ronson from 2018). The modelled band runs from the lowest tempo the entry states — \"~108 for moombahton\", the one reading it marks \"(documented)\" — up to the top of its house band, \"120-126 for the Silk City house project\". The third documented band, \"140-150 for the dancehall/trap material with a half-time feel\", is a different rhythmic family and is named here rather than folded in, because the compendium's rule is that families are picked and never blended. ⚠ INFERRED: the entry states 108 as a point and 120-126 as a band, so the 109-119 interior of the modelled range is a continuity choice, not a documented span; nothing below 108 is documented anywhere in the entry. The drums encode his stated vocabulary: \"dembow and baile-funk percussion — a syncopated kick-and-snare cell that leaves the backbeat implied — plus New Orleans bounce triplets and Miami-bass 808 patterns\", so the kick abandons the four-square grid for an anchor on 1 with a 0.42 tresillo bias, the snare keeps a 2&4 placement carrying the dembow figure as near-certain ghosts, and the perc bed is the widest in this section at five Latin and hand lanes. His stated view of dancehall as the terminus of house, soca, oldies, R&B and jazz is the map of that palette. `bass808` is `counter_riff` for the documented \"808 sub with short glides in the trap/dancehall mode\", so the filtered house sub of Silk City survives as the bassline. Harmony is \"the least important parameter in his work by design\" — two- or four-chord minor vamps — per the Hollertronix philosophy of \"disparate genres… smashed together for maximum attention-grabbing impact\". The lead palette is pitched flute, pan-pipe, marimba and chopped vocal. ⚠ The research says the tempo bands are partly convention-derived; that mark is repeated here, and every velocity, density and probability is INFERRED.",
